# Public keys allowed to log in as `toua.user` on every host in this flake.
#
# One key per line, in sshd's own authorized_keys format — `ssh-<type> <base64>
# [comment]` — so they can be pasted straight out of an existing
# ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, or appended with `ssh-copy-id`. Blank lines and lines
# beginning with `#` are ignored; nothing else is.
#
# This file is deliberately plaintext. These are public keys, so encrypting them
# with sops would buy nothing, and it would cost something: a sops secret is only
# decrypted at activation, but `authorizedKeys.keys` is built at evaluation time,
# so keys could not be read from one. Keeping them here also means they are baked
# into the system at build time — which matters on wall-e, where sshd is the only
# way in and a decryption failure would otherwise lock you out of a fresh box.
#
# Adding a key here grants login on every machine, wall-e included.
